          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: en effet",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "en effet — \"indeed; and that is because\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il est fatigué; en effet, il a travaillé toute la nuit. He is tired; indeed, he worked all night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It confirms or explains what came before; it does not mean in effect."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "effet comes through Old French effet from Latin effectus \"an effect, a result\" (EtymDB), from efficere \"to bring about\", built on facere \"to do, to make\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
