          "title": "You'll want to know: dès lors",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dès lors — \"from then on; consequently\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il a perdu son travail; dès lors, tout a changé. He lost his job; from then on, everything changed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two senses: from that moment on, and so. Dès lors que means given that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lors goes back through Old French to Vulgar Latin illā hōrā \"at that hour\" (EtymDB). dès \"from\" is usually traced to Latin dē ex \"from out of\"."
            }
          ]
        },
